## Running Instructions

### evaluation_runner.py — Single-Checkpoint Evaluation

This is the primary evaluation script. It loads ONE checkpoint, extracts embeddings, and runs selected `_eval_*` methods.

**Basic usage:**
```bash
python code/evaluation_runner.py \
  --checkpoint /path/to/checkpoint_best.pt \
  --eval_methods embedding_similarity \
  --eval_data_dir /mnt5/noy/fairseq/data/single_channel_1m/ \
  --max_eval_samples 100
```

**Multiple methods:**
```bash
python code/evaluation_runner.py \
  --checkpoint /path/to/checkpoint_best.pt \
  --eval_methods embedding_similarity knn_retrieval component_clustering repr_geometry \
  --eval_data_dir /mnt5/noy/fairseq/data/single_channel_1m/ \
  --max_eval_samples 500
```

**All methods at once:**
```bash
python code/evaluation_runner.py \
  --checkpoint /path/to/checkpoint_best.pt \
  --all_methods \
  --eval_data_dir /mnt5/noy/fairseq/data/labeled_data/ \
  --max_eval_samples 200
```

**With random weight baseline comparison:**
```bash
python code/evaluation_runner.py \
  --checkpoint /path/to/checkpoint_best.pt \
  --eval_methods embedding_similarity \
  --include_random_weights \
  --eval_data_dir /mnt5/noy/fairseq/data/single_channel_1m/ \
  --max_eval_samples 100
```

**Auto-discover and evaluate all best checkpoints:**
```bash
python code/evaluation_runner.py \
  --checkpoint_dir /mnt5/noy/fairseq/outputs \
  --best_only \
  --eval_methods embedding_similarity clustering \
  --eval_data_dir /mnt5/noy/fairseq/data/single_channel_1m/ \
  --max_eval_samples 100
```

**Specific run names only:**
```bash
python code/evaluation_runner.py \
  --checkpoint_dir /mnt5/noy/fairseq/outputs \
  --run_names 2026-01-07_21-50-07 2026-02-15_10-30-00 \
  --eval_methods embedding_similarity \
  --eval_data_dir /mnt5/noy/fairseq/data/single_channel_1m/ \
  --max_eval_samples 100
```

**Available `--eval_methods`:**
`embedding_similarity`, `noise_robustness`, `stack_similarity`, `signal_completion`, `validation_loss`, `label_regression`, `clustering`, `knn_retrieval`, `component_clustering`, `repr_geometry`, `downstream_probing`, `fewshot`, `component_detection`, `parameter_verification`, `baselines`, `efficiency`, `attention`, `failure_analysis`, `augmentation_invariance`

**Key flags:**
| Flag | Description |
|---|---|
| `--checkpoint <path>` | Path to a specific `.pt` checkpoint file |
| `--checkpoint_dir <path>` | Base directory to auto-discover checkpoints |
| `--eval_methods <m1> <m2> ...` | Which evaluation methods to run |
| `--all_methods` | Run all available evaluation methods |
| `--eval_data_dir <path>` | Dataset to evaluate on |
| `--max_eval_samples <N>` | Number of samples (default 100; use 1000+ for clustering) |
| `--include_random_weights` | Add random weight baseline (5-way comparison) |
| `--best_only` | Only evaluate `checkpoint_best.pt` files |
| `--latest_only` | Only evaluate the most recent checkpoint |
| `--custom_dataset_path <path>` | Additional dataset for 4-way comparison |
| `--dim_reduction pca tsne umap` | Dim reduction methods for clustering plots |
| `--debug` | Save debug plots of evaluated samples |

### run_full_evaluation.py — Multi-Checkpoint Orchestration

